Whitepaper v2.0.1: typography + uncited reference cleanup

Two LaTeX-only fixes flagged by Copilot review on PR #15, lifted out
into a small focused PR off main since PR #15 has diverged 47 commits
behind main and 16 commits ahead with substantial duplicated content.

Changes to agent-transactions-whitepaper.tex:

1. Drop the "(de Marneffe 2011)" parenthetical from §7.4.4 "Cost".
   The reference was the only mention in the document and was not in
   the bibliography, so it was an uncited claim. Remove rather than
   invent a bibitem.

2. Move the Youle-authorship footnote into the §7.4.5 subsubsection
   title via \protect\footnote{...}. Placing \footnote{} on a line
   after a sectioning command renders the marker on the next paragraph
   instead of attached to the heading; with \protect\footnote{} inside
   the title, the marker now sits with the section name.

3. Bump version "April 2026 / Version 2.0 (pre-print)" →
   "May 2026 / Version 2.0.1 (pre-print)". This is a typography patch,
   not a content revision, so the patch-level bump is appropriate.
   The v2.5 ProVerif rounds + redteam crypto isolation work remains
   queued in a separate stack and will land as v2.5 when ready.

The PDF was rebuilt locally with pdflatex (twice, for TOC stability)
and committed alongside the .tex/.aux/.out/.toc to keep the
checked-in artifact and source in sync.

No content changes to the paper's substance. No website code changes.


